	<key>readme</key>
	<string># Eject photo library

Open Alfred, type **ejp**, and press Return. Choose an image if several match.

Finds mounted disk images held open by Photos libraries. Tries a normal eject,
then gracefully stops only known Apple background services holding the selected
image open and retries. Other apps must be closed manually. No force eject,
force kill, permanent indexing changes, or administrator password.

Handles disk images and sparsebundles. Physical drives are outside this workflow.
Normal results and notifications are generic; volume names appear only when
needed to distinguish several matches.

Created by [nando rossi](https://nan.do).
[Buy me a coffee](https://buymeacoffee.com/nandorossi).

Source: https://github.com/nandorocker/eject-photo-library
</string>
